{"issues":[{"expand":"renderedFields,names,schema,operations,editmeta,changelog,versionedRepresentations","id":"103717","self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/issue/103717","key":"MC-209932","renderedFields":{"summary":null,"issuetype":null,"watches":null,"customfield_10070":null,"customfield_10061":"","created":"29/Dec/20 8:20 AM","customfield_10050":"","customfield_10051":null,"description":"<h3><a name=\"TheBug%3A\"></a><b>The Bug:</b></h3>\n\n<p>Sculk sensors only detect the last turtle egg being broken when being stepped on.</p>\n<h3><a name=\"StepstoReproduce%3A\"></a><b>Steps to Reproduce:</b></h3>\n<ul>\n\t<li>Place down four turtle eggs on the same block.</li>\n\t<li>Place down a sculk sensor nearby, stand on top of the turtle eggs, and wait for them to break.</li>\n\t<li>Take note as to whether or not sculk sensors only detect the last turtle egg being broken when being stepped on.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n<h3><a name=\"ObservedBehavior%3A\"></a><b>Observed Behavior:</b></h3>\n\n<p>Sculk sensors aren't actiavted.</p>\n<h3><a name=\"ExpectedBehavior%3A\"></a><b>Expected Behavior:</b></h3>\n\n<p>Sculk sensors would be activated.</p>\n<h3><a name=\"CodeAnalysis%3A\"></a><b>Code Analysis:</b></h3>\n\n<p>Code analysis by&nbsp;<a href=\"https://mojira.atlassian.net/secure/ViewProfile.jspa?accountId=Avoma\" rel=\"noreferrer\">Avoma</a>&nbsp;can be found below.</p>\n\n<p>The following is based on a decompiled version of Minecraft 1.18.2 using MCP-Reborn.</p>\n<div class=\"code panel\" style=\"border-width: 1px;\"><div class=\"codeHeader panelHeader\" style=\"border-bottom-width: 1px;\"><b>net.minecraft.world.level.block.TurtleEggBlock.java</b></div><div class=\"codeContent panelContent\">\n<pre class=\"code-java\"><span class=\"code-keyword\">public</span> <span class=\"code-keyword\">class </span>TurtleEggBlock <span class=\"code-keyword\">extends</span> Block {\n   ...\n &nbsp; <span class=\"code-keyword\">private</span> void decreaseEggs(Level $l, BlockPos $bp, BlockState $bs) {\n      $l.playSound((Player)<span class=\"code-keyword\">null</span>, $bp, SoundEvents.TURTLE_EGG_BREAK, SoundSource.BLOCKS, 0.7F, 0.9F + $l.random.nextFloat() * 0.2F);\n      <span class=\"code-object\">int</span> i = $bs.getValue(EGGS);\n      <span class=\"code-keyword\">if</span> (i &lt;= 1) {\n         $l.destroyBlock($bp, <span class=\"code-keyword\">false</span>);\n      } <span class=\"code-keyword\">else</span> {\n         $l.setBlock($bp, $bs.setValue(EGGS, <span class=\"code-object\">Integer</span>.valueOf(i - 1)), 2);\n         $l.levelEvent(2001, $bp, Block.getId($bs));\n      }\n\n   }\n   ...</pre>\n</div></div>\n<p>If we look at the above class, we can see that when the last turtle egg is broken, the <tt>destroyBlock()</tt> method is called. The <tt>destroyBlock()</tt> method then calls the <tt>gameEvent()</tt> method resulting in a vibration being produced. The problem here is that when there is more than one turtle egg occupying the same space, and one of them was to be destroyed, the <tt>gameEvent()</tt> method is never called, thus not detecting this action as a vibration.</p>\n<h3><a name=\"PotentialFix%3A\"></a><b>Potential Fix:</b></h3>\n\n<p>Simply calling the&nbsp;<tt>gameEvent()</tt> method where appropriate within this piece of code should resolve this problem. The \"BLOCK_DESTROY\" game event tag would be expected to be used here as the turtle eggs are destroyed.</p>","customfield_10054":null,"fixVersions":null,"customfield_10055":null,"resolution":null,"customfield_10047":"29/Dec/20 5:33 PM","customfield_10048":null,"labels":null,"customfield_10049":null,"attachment":[{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/135429","id":"135429","filename":"MC-209932.mp4","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/712020:fe0b28a2-a443-4748-adec-94acc213ea9e/5676b346-5dd0-49ca-b3b9-9eadab726d17/48","24x24":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/712020:fe0b28a2-a443-4748-adec-94acc213ea9e/5676b346-5dd0-49ca-b3b9-9eadab726d17/24","16x16":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/712020:fe0b28a2-a443-4748-adec-94acc213ea9e/5676b346-5dd0-49ca-b3b9-9eadab726d17/16","32x32":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/712020:fe0b28a2-a443-4748-adec-94acc213ea9e/5676b346-5dd0-49ca-b3b9-9eadab726d17/32"},"displayName":"Avoma","active":true,"timeZone":"Europe/London","accountType":"atlassian"},"created":"27/Feb/21 10:08 AM","size":"6.46 MB","mimeType":"video/mp4","content":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/135429"},{"self":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/135430","id":"135430","filename":"MC-209932.png","author":{"avatarUrls":{"48x48":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/712020:fe0b28a2-a443-4748-adec-94acc213ea9e/5676b346-5dd0-49ca-b3b9-9eadab726d17/48","24x24":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/712020:fe0b28a2-a443-4748-adec-94acc213ea9e/5676b346-5dd0-49ca-b3b9-9eadab726d17/24","16x16":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/712020:fe0b28a2-a443-4748-adec-94acc213ea9e/5676b346-5dd0-49ca-b3b9-9eadab726d17/16","32x32":"https://avatar-management--avatars.us-west-2.prod.public.atl-paas.net/712020:fe0b28a2-a443-4748-adec-94acc213ea9e/5676b346-5dd0-49ca-b3b9-9eadab726d17/32"},"displayName":"Avoma","active":true,"timeZone":"Europe/London","accountType":"atlassian"},"created":"06/Jun/21 3:59 AM","size":"608 kB","mimeType":"image/png","content":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/content/135430","thumbnail":"https://mojira.atlassian.net/rest/api/3/attachment/thumbnail/135430"}],"versions":null,"resolutiondate":"24/May/22 6:13 AM","issuelinks":null,"updated":"27/Aug/26 2:28 AM","status":null},"fields":{"summary":"Sculk sensors only detect the last turtle egg being broken when being stepped 